# Backend Folder Structure

Follow this structure under `src/` for all backend code:

```
src/
├── controllers/     # Request handlers (e.g. userController.js)
├── routes/          # Route definitions (e.g. userRoutes.js)
├── models/          # Data / domain models (e.g. userModel.js)
├── middleware/      # Express middleware (e.g. auth.js)
├── config/          # App and infra config (e.g. db.js, swagger.js)
├── seeders/         # DB seed scripts only (see below)
```

## Conventions

- **controllers**: Export functions that handle req/res; call models and return responses. One file per resource (e.g. `userController.js`).
- **routes**: Define Express routers and mount controller handlers. One file per resource (e.g. `userRoutes.js`). Wire routes in `app.js`.
- **models**: Export data shapes, validation, or DB access. One file per entity (e.g. `userModel.js`).
- **middleware**: Export Express middleware (e.g. auth, error handler). Use for cross-cutting concerns.
- **config**: Export configuration (DB connection, env-based options, Swagger, etc.). No business logic.
- **seeders**: All database seeding lives under `src/seeders/`. One file per seed concern (e.g. `seedRoles.js`); optional `index.js` to run seeds in order. Do not place seed scripts in `controllers/`, `routes/`, or ad-hoc paths.

When adding a new feature (e.g. "user"), create or update the relevant file in each layer: model → controller → routes, and add middleware only if needed. Add or extend seeders when initial/reference data must be loaded for dev or environments that expect seeded data.
